This plan is much better and I approve the overall architecture.

Using a HeaderAuthenticationFilter to populate the Spring Security SecurityContext is the correct enterprise approach.

Using @AuthenticationPrincipal instead of manually reading headers in every controller is also the correct approach.

Before implementation, I want to make a few architectural improvements so that the User Service remains scalable and reusable across the entire LMS.

===========================================================
GENERAL
===========================================================

Analyze the existing user-service before making any changes.

Do NOT regenerate the project.

Do NOT rewrite unrelated code.

Modify ONLY user-service.

===========================================================
USER PRINCIPAL
===========================================================

Create a reusable UserPrincipal class.

It should contain

userId

email

role

authorities

The UserPrincipal should be reusable by every microservice in the future.

===========================================================
HEADER FILTER
===========================================================

The HeaderAuthenticationFilter should ONLY

• Read trusted headers

• Create UserPrincipal

• Populate SecurityContext

• Continue the filter chain

It must NOT contain business logic.

===========================================================
METHOD SECURITY
===========================================================

Enable method-level security.

Use

@EnableMethodSecurity

Use

@PreAuthorize

wherever role-based authorization is required.

Avoid manual role comparisons inside controllers.

===========================================================
CONTROLLER
===========================================================

Controllers should remain lightweight.

Controllers should

Validate request

Read authenticated principal

Call service

Return response

No business logic should exist inside controllers.

===========================================================
SERVICE
===========================================================

The service layer should receive

authenticatedUserId

from the controller.

All business rules must remain inside the service layer.

===========================================================
PROFILE RULES
===========================================================

A user can create only one profile.

A user can update only their own profile.

A user can delete only their own profile.

Admin can manage every profile.

Students and instructors must never access another user's profile.

===========================================================
ADMIN APIS
===========================================================

Restrict

GET /users

GET /users/search

GET /users/{id}

PUT /users/{id}

DELETE /users/{id}

to ROLE_ADMIN only.

===========================================================
SWAGGER
===========================================================

Document Bearer Authentication.

Document the /me endpoints.

Clearly document that

X-User-* headers are injected automatically by the API Gateway.

Clients must never send these headers manually.

